class:: GendyInterp
summary:: Four renderers for identical stochastic breakpoint histories
categories:: UGens>Generators>Stochastic>GENDY
related:: Guides/Stochastica, Guides/Stochastica-GENDY, Classes/Gendy1991

description::
strong::Post-Xenakis interpolation extension.::

A first-order DSS engine with explicit interpolation. Brown's IDSS offers linear, cosine and square curves (2005, section 4.2); Bhob Rainey's sc3-plugins Gendy4 and Gendy5 explore cubic and non-interpolated rendering. Sources: link::https://research-repository.griffith.edu.au/server/api/core/bitstreams/dc7c2e4f-bc64-58c7-8ee0-bd7d219f39a2/content:: and link::https://github.com/supercollider/sc3-plugins/blob/main/source/BhobUGens/BhobNoise.cpp::.

Stochastica defines hold, linear, cosine and cubic Hermite modes explicitly. Hermite uses zero tangents at both endpoints: its blend is t*t*(3-2*t), with no overshoot. Cosine uses (1-cos(pi*t))/2. Hold keeps the left endpoint for the entire segment and deliberately jumps. Modes 1–3 join the actual endpoints, including across cycles. This is not an exact Gendy4 renderer or a claim about Brown's unspecified square curve.

All modes consume the same innovations and durations for equal controls and seeds. Interpolation shapes the rendered spectrum while leaving the stochastic history unchanged. Mode changes wait for segment boundaries; switching out of hold can still introduce a jump. Shape parameters are fixed at one.

The oscillator remembers one amplitude and one incoming duration per point. Updates occur once per waveform cycle, in index order; a newly evolved first point connects from the actual previous cycle endpoint. Durations are fractional sample counts with carried remainder and a one-sample minimum. High settings therefore saturate the achievable frequency range. There is no antialiasing, automatic DC removal or loudness normalization. Start quietly; the examples use LeakDC and a short fade.

Construction/reset starts amplitudes at zero and durations at the midpoint of their bounds. Motion builds an audible waveform over the first cycles; zero amplitude mobility at construction stays silent. A later freeze retains the evolved waveform. Reset can deliberately interrupt continuity. Invalid selectors and numeric controls are conditioned to documented finite bounds; non-finite frequencies use 100/1000 Hz defaults.

Like vanilla link::Classes/Gendy1::, linear mode renders remembered stochastic breakpoints. GendyInterp exposes the rendering choice and keeps the same local history across all four modes.

